  "query_preview": "..\n(Wednesday through Monday)\nIssued at 1201 AM CST Tue Nov 17 2026\n\nA dry wand warmer pattern will prevail across West Central Texas\nfor mid week into the weekend. Upper level trough over the western\nUS will produce southwest flow aloft across the area, with the\nmain energy north of the area. Temperatures will gradually warm\nwith more sunshine, with temperatures reaching to near 70 by\nFriday. A weak shortwave will rotate north of the area for\nSaturday, with surface winds swinging a little more to the\nsouthwest as it passes. Thus, Saturday will be the warmest day\nwith highs in the low to mid 70s. Pacific cold front passes for\nSunday and drops temperatures back into the 60s. \n\nA stronger shortwave is set to move into the Southern Plains for\nearly next week, with a surface trough moving across the area\nSaturday night. Model blends are suggesting an area of convection\nwith as this surface trough passes with at least chance POPs on\nMonday night.",
